    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class with `@Test` methods, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured `OWNER_CREATED` audit event while keeping the existing human-readable audit line intact.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/OwnerPrimaryIdentifier.java`** (new) \u2014 a model-level \"single source of truth\" helper (matching the project's `MembershipNumber.of(owner)` / `OwnerIdentity.of(owner)` convention) that returns the owner's *current primary identifier*. Today it returns `customerCode`; when the customer code is later unified into the member id, only this one method changes and the event follows automatically.\n\n2. **`rest/function/owner/OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** (new) \u2014 an immutable `record` for the structured event with components in canonical order `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event}`, with the `event` fixed to `\"OWNER_CREATED\"`.\n\n3. **`rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`** (edited) \u2014 after emitting the existing audit line, it now builds an `OwnerCreatedEvent` and logs it as JSON on the same `AUDIT` logger. `seq` comes from a process-wide `static AtomicLong` (`incrementAndGet()`), giving a monotonically increasing value across creates; the identifier comes from `OwnerPrimaryIdentifier.of(owner)`. Serialization uses the project's Jackson 3 (`tools.jackson`) `JsonMapper`.\n\nThe emitted event looks like:\n```\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nThe acceptance test `coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` (which asserts an AUDIT line contains `OWNER_CREATED`, the owner id, and the `customerCode`) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
